{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_013AMiKTmcP5wdX3BySoPF1j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThis project generates Go implementations of Unix utilities from formal specifications derived from C source code, then verifies them via differential testing against GNU reference binaries. The four-stage pipeline: extract (C source) → specify (PRD + use case) → synthesize (mage-claude-orchestrator) → verify (differential tests).\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Architecture**: Human operator authors PRDs and use cases; orchestrator generates Go code in `cmd/` and `pkg/`; `pkg/testutils` runs differential tests against Homebrew GNU binaries. Generation targets are only `cmd/` and `pkg/` (magefiles/, docs/, .cobbler/, .claude/ are excluded per DD7).\n\n**Implementation state**: Working branch has specs but no generated Go code. Prior generated code (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge) lives at generation-merged tags, not the working branch — so code status for all use cases on the working branch is \"not started.\"\n\n**Current release**: `rel00.0` — Batch 0, foundational infrastructure. All four use cases are `spec_complete` / code `not started`.\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 use cases, excluding already-open issue #282 (pkg/testutils, rel00.0-uc004):\n- `rel00.0-uc001-magefiles` → generation target is `cmd/version` only (DD7); magefiles/ itself is excluded\n- `rel00.0-uc002-format` → `pkg/format/` library\n- `rel00.0-uc003-sys` → `pkg/sys/` library\n\nCanonical order (P8): libraries before consumers, alphabetical tie-break → `pkg/format` (uc002) before `pkg/sys` (uc003) before `cmd/version` (uc001). One task limit means I propose `pkg/format` first.\n\n`pkg/format` has no internal dependencies (no dependency on `pkg/sys`). It is a pure formatting utilities library. Implementation only (P2 separates tests).\n\n## Step 4: Proposed Task\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement pkg/format column alignment, ANSI color codes, and size formatting (rel00.0-uc002)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/prd004-format.yaml (if path does not exist, use Glob on docs/specs/product-requirements/ to locate the pkg/format PRD, then read it)\"\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml\n      - \"docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component section and design decisions 3, 7)\"\n      - go.mod\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/column.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Column alignment for tabular output -- rename to match primary exported type from PRD if different\"\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"ANSI color codes for file types and permissions -- rename to match primary exported type from PRD if different\"\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Human-readable size formatting (bytes to K/M/G) -- rename to match primary exported type from PRD if different\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement column alignment for tabular output (ls -l style) per the pkg/format PRD requirements -- exported API and type names must match the PRD exactly\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color codes for file types (regular, directory, symlink, executable, special) and permission bits per the pkg/format PRD requirements\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement human-readable size formatting converting raw byte counts to K/M/G form per the pkg/format PRD requirements\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"pkg/format is a shared library -- it must export clean public APIs for use by cmd/ packages and must not import cmd/ packages or pkg/testutils (ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3)\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"File names must be derived from the primary exported types specified in the PRD, not from the package name -- e.g. if the primary type for column alignment is AlignedTable, the file is table.go (ARCHITECTURE.yaml P7)\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"pkg/format has no external dependencies beyond the Go standard library; golang.org/x/sys is only used in pkg/sys, not pkg/format (ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology_choices)\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"All output targets LC_ALL=C semantics; no locale-aware collation or character classification is required (ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD6)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/... succeeds with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Column alignment function produces correctly padded multi-column output that matches ls -l tabular style as defined in the PRD\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"ANSI color functions return correct ANSI escape codes for each file type and permission combination as defined in the PRD\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Size formatting function converts byte counts to human-readable K/M/G form with rounding and threshold behavior matching the PRD specification\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"golangci-lint ./pkg/format/... passes with no warnings\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19123,"cache_read_input_tokens":15967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19123},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"43fae435-4a39-403d-b715-52249946b0a6","uuid":"99fbebc8-b51e-42a6-85ec-a513cb47f7df"}
